-- toluene, the third agreement case, and the second place where the peak count falls below the class
-- count. Atoms: 0 the ring carbon bearing the methyl, 1 the methyl carbon with hydrogens 2 to 4, then
-- the ring: 5 and 7 the carbons next to it with hydrogens 6 and 8, 9 and 11 the next pair with hydrogens
-- 10 and 12, 13 the far carbon with hydrogen 14. Both symmetries are proper -- the methyl rotation and
-- the two-fold ring rotation -- so the two readings agree on four classes.
num-tol-obs : List Nat
num-tol-obs = cons 2 (cons 3 (cons 4 (cons 6 (cons 8 (cons 10 (cons 12 (cons 14 nil)))))))
